            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0246" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.01/262b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-11">March 11, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. Reference your 48, March 10. The story of our request to Ireland for removal
                    of Axis representatives broke in London yesterday and was immediately headlined
                    in Washington papers. We decided therefore that the text of our note should be
                    given to the press at once. We telephoned Winant to inform the British and, in
                    order to save an extra call, asked him to telephone you. As soon as it was
                    decided to publish the note we also informed the Irish Legation. Brennan decided
                    to release the Irish note and we arranged an hour agreeable to the Legation for
                    the release of both notes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
